:649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-26T13:37:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T10:07:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested on Godot v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4] – issue reproducible. Not tested on other versions.\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS Sequoia 26.5, Apple M4, 16GB, Godot v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4]\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen an HTTP request is actively downloading data and the user quits the application, Godot becomes unresponsive and hangs indefinitely. The application requires force quit to terminate.\n\nThis occurs consistently when opening an asset library (which triggers remote HTTP requests) and immediately exiting while downloads are still in progress.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a scene or interface that initiates an HTTP request (e.g., an asset library that downloads remote resources)\n2. While the request is still in progress (download not yet complete), quit the application\n3. Godot becomes unresponsive and hangs indefinitely\n4. The application requires force quit to terminate\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A\n\n[Godot crash log.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28266886/Godot.crash.log.txt)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119782/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url"